language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Recover the weights of n bales of hay from the multiset of the weights of all pairs of bales (the pairwise sums, given in sorted order, not matched to pairs).
given n : int(1..)
given weights_dim1 : int(1..)
given weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..weights_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ the pair (PI[k], PJ[k]) with PI[k] < PJ[k] is the k-th pair of bale indices, in the order of the pair list
letting PI = [ i | i : int(1..n), j : int(1..n), i < j ]
letting PJ = [ j | i : int(1..n), j : int(1..n), i < j ]
find bales : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..sum(weights))
$ perm[k] is the position in the given weights list that holds the weight of the k-th pair of bales
find perm : matrix indexed by [int(1..weights_dim1)] of int(1..weights_dim1)

such that
$ every pair of bales is matched to exactly one of the given pair weights (the pair weights are a permutation of the list)
allDiff(perm),
$ the weight of each pair of bales is the sum of the weights of its two bales
forAll k : int(1..weights_dim1) . weights[perm[k]] = bales[PI[k]] + bales[PJ[k]]
